BHClusterTagging
================

This thorn supplies CarpetX's `EstimateError` routine with the tagging
criterion used by GRChombo's
`ImprovedChiPunctureExtractionTaggingCriterion`.

It tags:

* spherical regions around configured extraction radii until each radius has
  its requested refinement level; and
* nested cubical regions around the effective puncture groups exported by
  PunctureTracker.

PunctureTracker controls whether nearby punctures are grouped and the
mass-scaled distance used to identify mergers.  Its group positions are
mass-weighted and its group masses are sums of puncture masses, matching the
GRChombo TrackMergers input to the criterion.

Important parameters are `extraction_radii`, `extraction_levels`,
`minimum_horizon_points`, `bh_margin_factor`, and `num_nested_levels`.
Refinement levels are zero based: requesting extraction level N tags levels
0 through N-1.

When this thorn is active, CarpetX constructs the fresh hierarchy by
regridding from level zero. This lets AMReX cluster the BH-cluster tags and
project its resulting fine boxes back through the parent levels with the
configured proper-nesting buffer, analogous to Chombo's MeshRefine pass. The
complete hierarchy is built before `CCTK_POSTRESTRICTINITIAL`, where
BHClusterX performs its nonlinear initial-data solve.

For Chombo-style evolution regridding, set a nonzero
`CarpetX::regrid_intervals` entry for each desired base level, for example:

```
CarpetX::regrid_intervals = [0, 0, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 8, 16]
```

Entry `l` counts completed level-`l` steps and triggers one AMReX regrid from
level `l` through the finest level. A zero disables that base level; the
finest-level entry is ignored. If more than one interval is due at the same
time, the coarsest due level is used. With all entries zero, CarpetX retains
its existing `regrid_every` behaviour. `CarpetX::tag_buffer_size` and
`CarpetX::grid_buffer_size` continue to control AMReX's tag and
proper-nesting buffers respectively.

For tagging diagnostics, set `BHClusterTagging::verbose = yes`. The thorn
then writes the PunctureTracker counts, each puncture's group/mass/position,
and every reconstructed tagging group once per `verbose_every` Cactus
iterations (default: every iteration).

For distributed tagging diagnostics, additionally set
`BHClusterTagging::verbose_rank_inputs = yes` and
`BHClusterTagging::verbose_coverage = yes`. The first emits a compact input
fingerprint on every MPI rank; the second emits each local AMR component's
union tag count and nonzero per-group tag counts before AMReX clusters the
tags into boxes. Both use `verbose_every` as their reporting interval.
